From 825deef32cd2a2473470ba4ff0da6f7e1f4a7b27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:19:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] After the vote: two family devotions, hidden until James
 reads them (U11)

"When the Grown-Ups Voted Differently" (Matthew 10:2-4) and "Praying for
Leaders We Did Not Choose" (1 Timothy 2:1-4) in
client/public/family-devotions-world.json, the weekly shape with younger and
older questions, BSB verbatim, and a line for the grown-ups to
/help/politics. Each speaks to both sides of the table in turn (two labelled
paragraphs under Talk).

One flag hides them: "live": false. While it is false the family index has
no row for them (so no page, no prerendered head, no sitemap entry, no
library tab), the year map does not pin them, and their ids are not frozen;
the family and politics gates still check every line. Setting it true and
running the freeze, the index and the year map (scripts/lib/family-
devotion-file.mjs) publishes them through The Table: their own pages, a
"The world we live in" tab in the library, and tonight's devotion for the
weeks of November 8 and 15, 2026 (pinned in family-year-overrides.json,
waiting until then).

Gates: validate-family reads strand files ({ live, devotions }), keeps ids
unique across hidden and live, refuses a year map naming a hidden devotion
and a frozen id hidden again. validate-politics (scripts/lib/
family-politics.mjs) holds a politics devotion's two sides to its 55% word
band, refuses one side only, and refuses a devotion that talks about voting
without the mark. The year map lets a pin before its first year expire with
a note, so moving FIRST_YEAR on never fails on these.

Family.tsx is untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
